{number: 150}
{title: Tell Me the Old, Old Story}
{key: C}

{start_of_verse: 1}
[C] Tell me the Old, Old Story,
Of [F] unseen things a-[C] bove,
Of [G7] Jesus and His glory,
Of [C] Jesus and His love:
Tell me the story simply,
As [F] to a little [C] child,
For [F] I am weak and [C] weary,
And [G7] helpless and de-[C] filed.
{end_of_verse}

{start_of_chorus}
[G7] Tell me the Old, Old [C] Story,
[F] Tell me the Old, Old [C] Story,
[F] Tell me the Old, Old [C] Story,
Of [G7] Jesus and His [C] love.
{end_of_chorus}

{start_of_verse: 2}
[C] Tell me the story slowly,
That [F] I may take it [C] in,
That [G7] wonderful redemption,
God's [C] remedy for sin;
Tell me the story often,
For [F] I forget so [C] soon,
The [F] "early dew" of [C] morning
Has [G7] passed away at [C] noon.
{end_of_verse}

{start_of_verse: 3}
[C] Tell me the story softly,
With [F] earnest tones and [C] grave;
Re-[G7] member, I'm the sinner
Whom [C] Jesus came to save:
Tell me the story always
If [F] you would really [C] be,
In [F] any time of [C] trouble,
A [G7] comforter to [C] me.
{end_of_verse}

{start_of_verse: 4}
[C] Tell me the same old story,
When [F] you have cause to [C] fear
That [G7] this world's empty glory
Is [C] costing me too dear;
Yes, and when that world's glory
Is [F] dawning on my [C] soul,
Tell [F] me the Old, Old [C] Story:
"Christ [G7] Jesus makes thee [C] whole."
{end_of_verse}
